        "title": "Organizational Design - Mintzberg, Matrix vs Hierarchy, Conway's Law",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Org design is the choice of how to divide and coordinate work. Every organizational structure is a set of tradeoffs between efficiency and flexibility, depth and breadth, control and autonomy. Mintzberg's configurations provide the best taxonomy of how organizations actually look. Conway's Law adds the essential tech-org insight: your system architecture will mirror your communication structure whether you intend it or not."
